      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p3_b7",
      "text": "(1)\nThe weights \u03b1j \u22650 are selected on a validation split to\nreach a target structural coherence distribution, rather than\nto optimize a task-specific objective, and to avoid collapsing\ngraphs to trivial structures. We emphasize small graphs\nto keep overhead low. In practice, graphs with three to six\nnodes and a handful of edges suffice to detect common struc-\ntural failures such as unsupported leaps or self reference.\nThe score is normalized per dataset so that its range aligns\nwith the semantic score scale used later in the shaped reward.\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.08,
        101.59,
        543.18,
        219.12
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1228,
        406,
        2172,
        876
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 545,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p3_b8",
      "text": "Semantic score. The semantic score balances task success\nand faithfulness against hallucination penalties. It is com-\nputed from node level verification and task specific metrics.\nWe use a linear combination for transparency and stability:\n",
      "bbox": [
        306.97,
        233.01,
        543.19,
        278.92
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1227,
        932,
        2172,
        1115
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 239,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p3_b9",
      "text": "ssem(x, y) = \u03b21qfact(x, y) + \u03b22qtask(x, y) \u2212\u03b23qhall(x, y).\n",
      "bbox": [
        311.2,
        288.77,
        537.7,
        299.86
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1244,
        1155,
        2150,
        1199
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMMI10",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 58,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p3_b10",
      "text": "(2)\nHere qfact aggregates correctness of atomic claims, qtask\nis a standard metric such as exact match for mathemat-\nics or Recall-Oriented Understudy for Gisting Evaluation\n(ROUGE) for summarization, and qhall penalizes unsup-\nported or contradicted entities. Coefficients \u03b2j \u22650 are\ntuned on a held out set to match desired calibration and\nfaithfulness targets. A linear form avoids overfitting and re-\nduces the risk of gradient explosions that can occur with ag-\ngressive nonlinearities. If a domain lacks reliable automatic\nmetrics, qtask can be replaced by scores from a calibrated\nLLM judge or dropped entirely. The score is standardized\nper domain to a common numerical range so that it mixes\npredictably with the topology score in the shaped reward.\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.11,
        301.08,
        543.1,
        466.46
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1228,
        1204,
        2172,
        1865
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 757,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p3_b11",
      "text": "Uncertainty and pair weighting.\nUncertainty integrates\nepistemic dispersion from re elicited graphs and aleatoric\nambiguity in node verification. The top level combination\nis:\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.44,
        480.75,
        541.44,
        526.67
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1229,
        1923,
        2165,
        2106
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 175,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p3_b12",
      "text": "u(G) = \u03bbepiuepi(G) + \u03bbaleuale(G),\n\u03bbepi, \u03bbale \u22650.\n(3)\n",
      "bbox": [
        316.45,
